<title>ITALY: San Paolo,Santander buy Finconsumo.</title>
<headline>San Paolo,Santander buy Finconsumo.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Istituto Bancario San Paolo di Torino and Spain's Banco Santander will take control of Italian consumer credit company Finconsumo Spa with a 40 per cent stake each.</p>
<p>San Paolo, which already holds 20 percent of Finconsumo, said in a statement the acquisition concerned 15 million shares at 2,600 lire each, valuing the company at 65 billion lire.</p>
<p>San Paolo will purchase a further 20 percent from other shareholders while Banco Santander will take a direct 40 percent stake.</p>
<p>Finconsumo's other shareholders will be Cab with 10 percent, Insel with five percent and Banca di Credito del Piemonte with five percent.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
